        "text": "When you invest in something, you hope to get a return on that investment. This means you'll get back the money you put in, plus extra. You could invest in a small business, house or financial asset with a plan to sell it later at a profit. If you invest well, you might even be able to double or triple your initial capital. While a trader also wants to make a return, they do this over a much shorter period. So while a trader might buy the same cryptocurrency as an investor, traders are looking to make gains from short or mid term price changes. Traders frequently enter and exit positions to generate smaller returns over many trades. In contrast, investors play the long term game.",
        "start": 640,
        "end": 44170,
        "confidence": 0.99484247,
        "channel": null,
